# --- Project artefacts (regenerated, never tracked) ---
# Root-anchored: a bare `data/` would also match src/bkrobust/data/.
/results/*
!/results/.gitkeep
# The breakdown-radius demonstration's outputs ARE deliverables: report.md
# cites them and they are small CSV/JSON. Everything else under results/ is
# regenerated experiment output and stays untracked.
!/results/breakdown_radius_demo/
# Axis A / Axis B session outputs are deliverables too: the pre-registration,
# per-instance rows and manifests are cited by report_synth_and_search.md.
!/results/synth/
!/results/search/
# Session 2 (Axis B deep) outputs are deliverables cited by
# report_axisb_deep.md and THEOREMS.md.
!/results/axisb2/
!/results/axisb3/
!/results/axisb4/
!/results/axisa2/
!/results/axisa3/
# Stage 0 of the evaluation plan: the free rule and the claim-unit radius on the
# committed axisa3 rows, cited by docs/EVALUATION_PLAN.md.
!/results/stage0/
# Phase B: the observables-only candidate frame, its status composition under
# each knowledge source, and the first-failing retraction sets.
!/results/frame/
# The frozen questionnaire, the supplier answers and the knowledge they became.
# The response cache is regenerable from the questionnaire and stays untracked.
!/results/elicit/
/results/elicit/cache/
# The certificate ledger.
!/results/ledger/
# The estimated-CPDAG panel (P-EST, Table 7). The learned graphs are small JSON
# and the panel's substrate; samples regenerate from their seeds.
!/results/pest/
# The substrate of Table 2: sortability probes on the Gaussian tier, the
# per-network structure table and the written decisions on the fixtures.
!/results/substrate/
# Measurement M1: the knowledge interval, the null radius and their bands, with the
# pre-registration, the per-row and per-replicate outputs and the tables built on them.
!/results/interval/
/data/
/checkpoints/
*.pt
*.ckpt
*.pth
*.safetensors
*.npz
